content.thinking:
The "exited" revival test fails because the auto-done path doesn't actually set status to "exited" in this test. Looking at the test:

```js
const { state, artifactDir } = makeState({ outputContent: "result" });
mod.interactiveSubagentRegistry.set(state.id, state);

mod.pollArtifactChanges({} as any);
expect(state.autoDoneForTurnAt).toBeDefined();
expect(state.status).toBe("exited"); // auto-done marked it terminal  // ← fails here
```

The test calls `pollArtifactChanges` once and expects status to be "exited". But the actual code in the poller uses `deriveInteractiveSubagentStatus` from interactive-tmux.ts which I haven't updated on this branch. The current `pruneDeadInteractiveSubagents` (called by the poller) only sets status to "exited" on `done` event + pane dead. With the mock tmux making the pane "alive" (via display-message success), the status would be "running" or "idle" depending on events.

But wait, this is a DIFFERENT auto-done path. The auto-done is in `pollArtifactChanges` itself, not from the artifact event + pane liveness. Let me look at the auto-done logic.

